# Expected text derived by hand from Language ch. 10 ("a lowercase letter or `_` begins a
# value, an uppercase letter a function, constructor, type or trait").
# `case-mark` at `<-`: a hold's name is a value, so `$Count` is refused as `let W = 3` is;
# `!inc` and `$total` are legal. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to
# change.
emit Ui.*

@counter: @unit
@counter:
    !inc <- Ui.Button($label=$"+")
    $Count <- 0 then $Count + 1 on !inc
    $total <- 0 then $total + 2 on !inc
    Ui.Label($text=$"{$Count} {$total}")
